text:
claire: Quick design review for the "Nightshift" dark theme tweaks. Main goals: make 11px inline tokens readable and clarify multi-series charts on dashboards.

ben: Can you list the specific failures you saw in staging?

claire: 1) model tags at 11px fade into panel bg. 2) 5+ series charts — two lines look identical at glance. 3) keyboard focus ring almost invisible on modal overlays.

yumi: Agree re: focus. Also codeblock gutters use near-black stroke that disappears on some monitors.

claire: Proposed changes: bump small-token luminance + add subtle translucent backdrop for inline tokens; reserve 2 saturated accent colors for alerts; add patterned strokes (dot/dash) + small shape markers for charts. Sample CSS below.

```css
:root[data-theme="nightshift"]{
  --panel-bg: #091016;
  --token-small: #e9f3f6;
  --token-backdrop: rgba(7,12,16,0.32);
  --accent-alert: #ff6a5a;
  --accent-warn: #ffd36b;
}
/* chart: map index -> (color, pattern, marker) */
```

mike: Patterns + markers are solid. For SVG we can map stroke-dasharray + marker-end. Also consider legend compact mode with icons.

ben: Small note: don't brighten everything; use .token-small only for <=13px or .inline-token class. Keeps mood intact.

claire: Yes — will scope to .inline-token and .table-token. Also keep comments muted via italics instead of raising contrast.

theme-bot: Preview built: https://staging.redwood-inference.internal/preview/nightshift-contrast-1785 — includes token backdrops, chart patterns, and focus adjustments.

yumi: I'll run a quick 8-person microtest (identify series & copy inline token). Will share results tomorrow.

mike: One dev nit: ensure CSS variables map to chart lib config so theme toggles update charts without a full reload.

claire: Thanks all — I'll open the PR with the CSS, screenshots, and test plan. :thumbsup:
